The company has imposed some additional constraints on the logs received. This is how the new system works.

The factory receives event logs from two sensors. The logs can be merged only if both sensors share at least one common event ID.

Processing rules:

Check whether the two logs contain at least one common value.
If no common value exists, print "Invalid".
Otherwise:
combine both logs,
remove duplicate event IDs,
sort the final list in ascending order.
